<title>BRAZIL: Telemig Jan-Feb net 50.4 mln reais.</title>
<headline>Telemig Jan-Feb net 50.4 mln reais.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian state-owned telecom Telemig, a unit of federally owned Telebras serving Minas Gerais state, released the following preliminary financial results for January and February.</p>
<p>			Jan-Feb 1997</p>
<p>Gross Oper Revs     265.4 million</p>
<p>Net Oper Revs	 203.7 million</p>
<p>Oper profit	    66.7 million</p>
<p>Pre-tax profit	 66.6 million</p>
<p>Net profit	     50.4 million</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures are in Brazilian reais and not adjusted for inflation.</p>
<p>No comparative two-month results for 1996 were given.</p>
<p>The company said fixed lines totalled 1.53 million while cellular phones used amounted to 262,863.</p>
<p>((-- James Craig, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485413))</p>
